{
  "name": "poly-commit",
  "description": "A high-performance Rust library for constructing and verifying polynomial commitment schemes (PCS) essential for zkSNARK protocols. It provides a modular framework for univariate, multivariate, and multilinear polynomials, implementing major primitives such as KZG10 (with Marlin and Sonic variants), Inner Product Arguments (IPA), and hash-based linear-code schemes like Ligero and Brakedown. The library emphasizes cryptographic properties like succinctness, extractability, and optional hiding through structured reference strings and batch verification techniques.",
